WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.900
The year is 2205 A.D.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.240
To annihilate the History Retrograde Army,
who scheme to alter history...

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.870
...we, who were born from swords...

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.000
...engage in mortal combat today as well!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:47.770
"Touken Ranbu Hanamaru S2"

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.100
Master, we brought some flowers.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.180
Osayo, Kousetsu-<i>niisama</i>, and I grew them.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.350
It will bring you tranquility.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.770
"This anime is about the
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.610
of a certain group of
Sword Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.120
Urashima!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.040
This is bad.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.190
Monoyoshi!

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.860
Right!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.730
--Take that!
--There!

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.780
Monoyoshi, thanks for earlier.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.240
You saved us!

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.040
You have my thanks, too.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.710
"59 - Wakizashi, Monoyoshi Sadamune"

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.170
I'm glad everyone's okay.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.500
Good work.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.710
Thanks for your hard work.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:19.170
But man, good thing that
boulder dropped when it did earlier.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.380
Yes, it was fortunate.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:26.390
Well, I've got to introduce
you to the others, too.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:31.190
Oh, as expected of the guy in
charge of the new Sword Warriors.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:34.190
Yeah, well. Let's go, Monoyoshi.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.560
Okay.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.360
He's gotten more cheerful lately, hasn't he?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.990
Oh, do you have a minute?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.870
This is Monoyoshi Sadamune. He's new.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.000
He just got back from his first battle. Right?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.710
Nice to meet you.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.840
I'm Uguisumaru. Nice to meet you.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.260
I'm Hirano Toushirou.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.550
Oh, let me make some tea.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.090
Oh, I was just getting thirsty.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.890
I can help.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.430
Thanks.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.810
Here you go.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.440
Thank you very much.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.230
No problem. I'm glad I could help.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.940
Oh?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.820
There are three tea stalks...

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.320
I guess that happens sometimes.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.990
I must be having good luck.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.660
Huh?! Isn't that a bit much?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.120
It's my first time seeing that.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.330
A lot of them are standing, huh?

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.090
Kasen, you here?

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.590
Oh, are you Monoyoshi?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:51.310
Yes! Nice to meet you.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.270
Um, can I help with anything?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.600
Then, can you bring in the dried laundry?

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.520
Yes, with pleasure!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.820
Then, take that basket...

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.660
Please, wait!

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.740
Let's chase after them.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.120
Yeah.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.080
They'll get dirty!

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.830
Please, wait! Please, wait!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.920
This happens sometimes, too, huh?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.840
You were lucky.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.260
Man, I can't believe that just happened!

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.230
Mor... tar...

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.320
I'm not a pestle!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.860
Oh, Kashuu-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.320
Shokudaikiri.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.360
What's up?

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.200
Actually, we're out of soy sauce.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.620
Can you buy some at the general store?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.700
Soy sauce, right? Sure.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.460
May I go with you?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:05.920
Mor... tar... Mor... tar... Mor... tar...

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.130
Don't come near me!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.690
All right, if that's the case,
then I'll skewer you!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.110
"Skewer Complete"

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.900
Yay!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.450
'Cause I'm only good at stabbing...

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.870
Then, I'll go back to preparing dinner.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:41.540
I'm counting on you two.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.670
Then, shall we go?

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.170
Yes.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.800
"General Store"

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.760
"If you win, you get one more"
"Smoke Card | You can win" "Shiny Stickers"

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.970
You all came, too?

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.470
Oh, is that a new Sword Warrior?

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.020
Nice to meet you.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:03.190
I'm Monoyoshi Sadamune, also called a
sword of protection for the Tokugawa family.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.610
You were a Tokugawa sword, too?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.780
Yes. And you are?

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:13.320
"58 - Tantou, Houchou Toushirou"

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.700
I'm Houchou Toushirou!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.910
I'm a Toushirou brother,
and I'm shaped like a kitchen knife.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.200
My master was also Lord Tokugawa Ieyasu.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.120
How about it? Isn't it amazing?

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.000
Oh, Atsushi, can I pull a string candy?

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.420
"String Candy"

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.670
Yeah, sure.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.210
You don't know him?

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.960
The Tokugawa family had many swords,

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.340
so I don't know all of them.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.760
Oh, yay!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.020
Congratulations!

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.560
You were very lucky.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.940
Nice! All right, I'll get one, too!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.980
"Big Winner"

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.230
Yes!

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.610
Congratulations to you, too.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.030
That's amazing.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.030
Then, we will, too...

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.950
"Winner"

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.200
Wow, we did great!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.250
We got so much candy!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.170
I hope we got some that
those back at the citadel like.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.710
Yeah.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.880
But man, everyone was lucky today.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.340
Speaking of which, you said earlier
you were a sword of protection...

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.260
Hey, how's it going, everyone?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.300
Oh, Kashuu-<i>san</i>.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.520
Huh? What are you doing?

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.020
We're looking for lucky four-leaf clovers.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.730
Lucky four-leaf clovers?

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.730
Hakata's trading stocks again,
so we wanted to give one to him.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:32.780
Trading stocks? We already saved
a lot of money. Isn't it enough?

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.030
A-Actually...

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.080
What's up, Ichi-<i>nii</i>?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.580
You seem really happy.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.170
Actually, Kasen invited me to tea, and...

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.510
Drink up.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.530
A mysterious luster like the twinkle of stars...

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.320
...that captivated me before I knew it.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:19.990
I'm glad you like it.
Would you like another cup?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.790
That's what happened.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.040
I've never been captivated by a teacup before,

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.370
but it was really beautiful.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.960
It'd be nice to give Ichi-<i>nii</i>...

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.340
...his own teacup.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.920
"Price"

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.880
But...

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.380
...it's pretty expensive.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.140
There's no way we can buy this...

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.060
No, it's not impossible.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:44.020
We can use my stock trading!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:49.150
And so, Hakata is working hard for all of us.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.730
Oh, I see.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.570
But we can't really find anything...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.360
Um, is this it?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.320
Oh, a four-leaf clover!

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.120
Oh, there's one here, too.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.790
Even though we were looking
this whole time without finding any.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.210
Oh, there's one here, too!

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.670
Hm? I wonder what this is...

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.630
All right, I think we're done.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:15.340
Oh? Are all of those four-leaf clovers?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.840
Yes!

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:21.510
Monoyoshi-<i>san</i>, Kashuu-<i>san</i>,
thank you for helping us look.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.060
I'm glad I could help.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.980
Well, tell Hakata I said hi.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.390
--Okay!
--Okay.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:36.240
There's a fight I definitely
can't lose right here...

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.610
"Buy"

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.450
Hakata, why don't you take a break?

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.610
Hakata!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.660
What is it?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.750
This is from all of us, to you.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.750
Wow, there's so much! Thanks!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.380
Also--

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.340
Go on, Gokotai.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:58.630
This is made of lucky four-leaf clovers.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.850
What, so many? Wow!

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.350
And I found an interesting plant, too.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.390
Huh? What is it?

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.270
Let's see it.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.270
What is that?

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.020
I've never seen it before.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.900
You can't eat that!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.280
This is a caterpillar fungus.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.570
Gokotai, I can't believe you knew that.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.820
It was in the reference book
Kasen-<i>san</i> gave me last year.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.870
It's a pretty valuable medicinal herb.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.370
Huh? Valuable?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.200
Then all of this will bring good luck!

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.120
Suddenly, I feel like I can win this!

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.130
Hakata, do your best!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.380
Turn our feelings into reality.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:41.550
Yeah, I'll definitely win with
this investment for Ichi-<i>nii'</i>s sake!

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:43.050
You're so reliable!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.800
We're leaving it to you, Hakata.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.140
"Buy"

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.260
Now, it's do-or-die!

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.600
Here I go!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.850
"Purchased"

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:59.110
You can do it! You can do it! You can do it!

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.900
They look like they're having fun.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:01.950
Yeah.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.490
"Hakata"
"You can do it"

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:07.700
--You can do it! You can do it!
--Oh, it's rising! It's rising!

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.580
Kashuu, Hasebe's calling you.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.000
I wonder what he wants...

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.250
Wha--?

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.380
What's happening? It's like
my good fortune is running away!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.090
It's getting lower and lower.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:22.680
Everyone, louder!

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:26.220
--You can do it! You can do it!
--Oh, it's coming back up!
--Hey, Ookurikara, where's Hasebe?

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.390
In the kitchen.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.890
Okay.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.930
Hey, wait a minute!

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:36.690
Oh no, it just keeps getting lower! Wait!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.400
I'm counting on you.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.980
Okay.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.690
Wow...

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.490
There it goes!

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.160
"Sell"

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.110
Here it comes!

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.700
"You can do it♡"
"You can do it!"

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.410
Here it is, here it is.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:13.390
It was no use...

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:15.770
Hakata...

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:19.690
We also share responsibility
for leaving it all to Hakata.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:24.950
Then, let's think together about
a way to make Hakata feel better!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.030
Good idea.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.160
Yeah, let's do it.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.950
I wonder what would be good?

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.200
Hmm...

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.870
Shall we ask someone
with a connection to him?

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.800
I see. Hakata, huh?

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.050
We thought maybe since you were
with the Kuroda family at the same time,

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.720
you might have a good idea.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.850
Well then, how about the Gion Yamakasa?

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.890
Yamakasa, huh?

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:58.060
Um, what is this "Yamakasa"?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:01.610
It's a festival held every year in Hakata.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:07.200
--It's a lively festival with a parade
of tall floats called "<i>yamakasa</i>."
--Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.160
I believe this is the
perfect season for<i> yamakasa</i>.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.040
Then, Hakata might have
fond memories and cheer up.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.120
Yes!

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.290
But a festival, huh...?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.000
It's good idea!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.630
Hasebe-<i>san</i>, please.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:27.590
All right. I'll talk to Master about it.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.430
--Thank you.
--Thank you very much.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:38.940
For the Yamakasa Festival, the large,
majestic floats are the main event.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:43.320
I'll make a great one for Hakata's sake!

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.030
Is this good here?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:49.280
Yeah! A festival's gotta have stalls!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.040
I'm looking forward to the festival!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.370
Sada-<i>chan</i>, what stall should we do?

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.630
A food one would be good, don't you think?

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.960
All of the food you make tastes great, Micchan!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.720
Since you say that,
I guess I'll have to do my best.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:15.600
Kousetsu-<i>niisama</i>, what stall shall we have?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.890
How about something like this?

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.650
I think that's good.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:37.490
It's not rising at all...

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.880
Hakata, how about a change of pace?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:49.210
But I don't know when the price'll rise again...

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.090
It's fine, it's fine!

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.590
What?

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:00.020
Wow, it's a <i>yamakasa</i>!

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.650
What do you think, Hakata?

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.360
Pretty good, huh?

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:08.070
It's my first time seeing such a large float.

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.150
I'm looking forward to it, too.

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:13.990
The place where you lived had
an amazing festival, huh, Hakata?

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.580
C-Can I help, too?

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.120
I have no reason to refuse!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.640
I'm coming in.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.390
Jeez...

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.060
"Festival"

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.100
Here. From Master.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.650
How is it? Does it look good?

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.070
Hasebe, thanks.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.990
Don't mention it.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.580
But the weather...

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.590
We're all ready!

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.220
Yeah!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.990
I wanted to have a <i>yamakasa</i> parade...

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.910
Well, we can do it once the rain lets up.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.830
Just have a little patience.

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:43.200
Don't be discouraged, Hakata.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.170
We have returned!

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.300
Oh, were you on an expedition?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.130
Yes!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.720
We heard from the others.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.840
We're preparing for a festival, right?

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.890
But the rain...

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.850
Oh, but it looks like it'll stop soon.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.350
Huh?

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:12.320
Yay! Yay!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:17.490
When you show up, Monoyoshi,
it's like something good always happens.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:21.740
Well, we always won when
I was brought along to a battle.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:25.120
That's why I was given the name,
Monoyoshi, which means "good luck."

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.040
I see.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.130
I wonder if I was able to bring good fortune?

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:48.060
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.350
The udon's ready.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.770
Okay, one cold-hot udon!

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.780
Thanks.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.900
Hey, Kara! What do you think? Isn't it good?

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:58.990
Yeah.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.540
It's cold at first, but still warm.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.460
Okay! Thanks for waiting!

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.060
Get that for me!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.470
Sure!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.890
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.020
"Candy Sculptures"

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.650
Ooh, candy sculptures!

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.570
There are candy apples, too.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.030
Yay!

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.200
Festivals really are the best!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.120
Kousetsu-<i>niisama</i>...

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.620
You're amazing...

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.540
Ka, ka, ka!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:58.460
July is also the season for Tanabata,
so we got some bamboo!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.100
I want to write a wish!

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.600
Apparently, the <i>tanzaku</i> strips for
Tanabata were originally not for wishes,

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.350
but for people to write the
goals they wanted to improve on.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:15.020
So we write what we want to improve on?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.860
I want to be better at dancing.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.610
I want to be better at preparing medicines.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.320
I want to be tougher.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.490
I want to be able to make delicious tea.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:33.500
Hmm... Maybe "I want to be cuter"?

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.930
It's not really something to improve on, but...

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:47.760
"I wish for Yasusada to become even stronger."

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:54.140
Yasusada, we're making another
fun memory while you're gone.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.060
Hurry up and come back.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.200
That'll do.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:08.240
"...for Kiyomitsu..."

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.920
Tamaya!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:21.960
I'm pretty sure there was a fan here...

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.130
"Hakata"

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.840
Oh, there it is!

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.510
I'm glad.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.970
Now to return to the festival.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:40.270
Tamaya!

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:49.280
"AWT48 will have a solo summer concert!!!"

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.580
What is this?

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:59.750
Oh? After I wrote it on the <i>tanzaku</i>,
I got better at dancing right away.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:03.380
That's right, I can... do it, too...

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.760
The <i>tanzaku</i> worked really well, huh?

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:09.350
Leave it to Nakigitsune to produce this!

00:22:09.350 --> 00:22:13.600
All right, I can't lose
to my little brothers, either.

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:15.480
Huh? What?

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:18.150
Wait, what?!

00:23:52.570 --> 00:23:54.910
Huh? What was that just now?

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:01.590
"Producer: Nakigitsune"
"More <i>Hanamaru</i> Next Week!!"
